    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nWith default mappings, even if |s| is diabled with \r\n```vim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x' }, 's', '<Nop>')``` \r\nas [described in the documentation](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-surround.txt#L573C3-L573C45) , the combination \"sa\" needs to be pressed within timeoutlen.\r\n\r\nHowever, for example combination \"dd\" does not. \n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn a text file containing text, press s. \r\nWait longer than timeoutlen.\r\nPress a.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nafter pressing iw) the word under cursor will be surrounded by ()\n\n### Actual behavior\n\niw) are inserted inside of the word. Because \"a\" acted like a normal nvim command.",
