            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is how mappings work in Neovim: if mapping contains more than one key press, each of them should be pressed no longer than 'timeoutlen' milliseconds after the previous. The documentation says that it will prevent occasional usage of built-in `s` action (which will delete character under cursor and start Insert mode) and it does exactly that.\r\n\r\nThere are more details in `:h map-typing`.\r\n\r\n> However, for example combination \"dd\" does not.\r\n\r\n`dd` is not a mapping created by user but keys for built-in action, which can behave differently.",
